new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c5793198
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/research/omega/momega1/HOST-7B-RUNTIME-HANDOFF.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# ALPHA exact 7B host candidate
+
+Candidate only. The [owner approval](HOST-7B-ADMISSION.md) authorizes the exact official 7B weights and existing reviewed llama-completion binary, with at most 8 GiB for the model inference job. The 1.5B reviewed tuple and its direct host transport remain unchanged. No 7B native inference, correctness, Android, or release acceptance is claimed here. Independent review is required before changing the 7B registry status or null review certificate.
+
+The larger GGUF allowance requires all six exact provenance fields; an altered field keeps the existing 2 GiB cap. The existing parser is still the sole format gate. The 7B-only immutable resource profile gives a 4,683,073,536-byte file ceiling, 7 GiB native virtual-address limit, and at most 8 GiB aggregate kernel cgroup memory with swap disabled. Fixed production transport actually sets the container to **7 GiB**, leaving **1 GiB** for the host caller's existing bounded context/request/response handling. The host provider never reads the weights. File hashing uses 1 MiB chunks and the header parser uses at most 32 MiB. The source task/canonical repair executor remains outside this inference container and unchanged.
+
+`getLocalModelResourceProfile({provenance,runtimeSha256})` in `scripts/continuum-local-model-pins.mjs` returns the frozen exact 7B profile or null. `assertLocalModelJobMemoryLimit(profile)` in the observation helper requires actual CGROUP2 controls, a private namespace root, parent in the same group, root-owned controls, memory.max <= 8 GiB and memory.swap.max = 0. The shared host group (16 GiB) blocks with `BLOCKED_LOCAL_JOB_MEMORY_LIMIT`. This is independent of genuine-model admission: `getReviewedLocalModelPair` still returns null for 7B.
+
+The existing default provider uses the fixed Docker job transport only for the exact 7B/runtime hash and LLAMA_CPP kind. It keeps per-request HMAC secrets on stdin and validates the same immutable original observation; injected transports cannot brand evidence. Transport pins the existing empty image by full immutable image ID, uses --pull=never, a fixed local Unix Docker endpoint, a private empty client configuration, explicit Node entrypoint, no network, no capabilities, no-new-privileges, user 1000, a read-only root, and a bounded tmpfs. Only trusted script/continuum source directories, public Node/libraries, and the three canonical regular configured files are mounted read-only. No Docker socket, HOME, Git metadata, caller checkout, credentials, or host environment enters the container. A finally block forcibly removes the named job even after client failure/timeout.
+
+The fixed outer seccomp allowlist permits trusted Node/bwrap bootstrap, local AF_UNIX and route-only AF_NETLINK; AF_INET/AF_INET6 socket creation and unlisted syscalls remain denied. clone3 returns ENOSYS. Docker system-path masking must be disabled so nested bwrap can mount a new proc filesystem for its private PID namespace. This does not grant capabilities or writable host mounts. The existing native seccomp, all namespace isolation, descriptor mounts, process cancellation and budgets remain active. The fixed 7B profile adds official same-binary `--no-repack` to avoid copying the 4.68 GB weights into a second repacked allocation; context 8192, output 1800, threads 2 and task call/time limits stay unchanged. Qwen ChatML/schema serialization is enabled only for the two known exact Qwen model hashes.
+
+New observation fields for 7B are `resourceProfileId`, `nativeAddressSpaceBytes`, `disableWeightRepacking`, and nested `jobMemoryLimit:{maxJobMemoryBytes,maxJobSwapBytes,enforcement:'CGROUP_V2'}`. The default provider requires the exact 7 GiB/zero-swap values, authenticates the full receipt, and freezes the nested object. Candidate observations remain HOST_INTEGRATION with verifiedModelExecution false.
+
+Non-secret 7B environment: `/workspace/momega1-local-model/qwen7b/runtime-env.json`. It preserves the existing public field names and points to the separately approved file and manifest; the original 1.5B environment is unchanged. No model is committed.
+
+Evidence is in `docs/evidence/momega1/runtime/7b`. Baseline 5feb1a93 produced four RED boundaries (manifest, profile API, ChatML, hard cap). Expanded host regressions cover the existing GGUF/provider/orchestrator path plus six new boundaries. Real Docker negative transport verifies the actual CLI rejects dummy weights and a mismatched full manifest without an observation. Docker synthetic process contracts are CONTRACT_TEST only. Early Docker logs preserve missing Node path, PID1/parent checks, missing tool symlinks, proc masking and noexec tmpfs failures. The final synthetic contract command uses **exec on its test-only tmpfs** to execute compiled C fixtures; production transport retains noexec tmpfs and uses only the fixed pinned host runtime mount. Neither fixture nor these bootstrap probes is evidence of model inference.
+
+Actual native runs remain deferred for QA/UI priority and independent challenger review. Required next evidence: full-file identity/format through the real helper, clean normal decoding, exact observed cgroup cap and combined container/host-caller memory, bounded cancellation, immutable model/runtime identity, and default-provider brand/forgery controls. Do not raise the resource cap if the first run fails.
